---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { url } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Segment a render for lighting"
  description="Separate a render into per-object and per-wall-plane selection masks for lighting work in post — light each region individually. Runs entirely in your browser."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Tools · Beta"
    title="Segment a render for lighting"
    lede="For the lighting pass in post-production. Upload a render and the tool separates it into solid flat-colour regions — each object, and each wall plane — so you can select and light each one individually in Photoshop, the way you would light them in the scene. Then you download the mask. Two ways to run it: free in-browser (the image never leaves your machine), or cloud AI (Gemini / GPT) with your own API key for cleaner separation — that one sends the image to the provider."
  >
    <p class="vi-block vi-def mt-2 text-[0.95rem] max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Dành cho khâu chỉnh sáng hậu kỳ. Tải lên một ảnh render, công cụ tách thành các vùng màu phẳng
      đặc — từng vật thể, và từng mảng tường theo hướng — để bạn chọn và chiếu sáng riêng từng vùng
      trong Photoshop, đúng như cách bạn xử lý ánh sáng trong scene. Rồi tải mặt nạ về. Có hai cách
      chạy: trong trình duyệt (miễn phí, ảnh không rời khỏi máy), hoặc AI đám mây (Gemini / GPT) bằng
      API key của bạn cho kết quả tách sạch hơn — cách này ảnh sẽ được gửi lên nhà cung cấp.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <div
    class="card p-4 mb-6 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl"
    style="border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warning) 40%, transparent)"
  >
    <strong style="color: var(--warning)">What it gives you, and where it stops.</strong>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted)">
      It turns the render into masks for a lighting pass: each object separated, and each wall plane
      split by orientation, so you can grade the light on every surface independently — a wall
      grazed here, an accent lifted there. The regions are lighting-independent: a shadow or a bright
      hotspot does not break an object into pieces. The in-browser engine is a geometric
      approximation, not a V-Ray object pass — very thin elements such as a slim light strip may
      still be missed. The cloud AI engines (Gemini / GPT) separate objects much more cleanly, but
      they redraw the matte rather than measure it, so always check edge alignment against the
      original before trusting a mask.
    </span>
    <p class="vi-block vi-def mt-2">
      Công cụ biến ảnh render thành mặt nạ cho khâu chỉnh sáng: tách riêng từng vật, và chia mỗi mảng
      tường theo hướng, để bạn chỉnh ánh sáng riêng cho từng bề mặt — chỗ này rửa tường, chỗ kia nhấn
      sáng. Các vùng không phụ thuộc ánh sáng: một vệt bóng hay điểm sáng chói không làm vỡ một vật
      thành nhiều mảnh. Engine trong trình duyệt là xấp xỉ hình học, không phải VRay object pass —
      vật rất mảnh (ống đèn) vẫn có thể bị bỏ sót. Engine AI đám mây (Gemini / GPT) tách vật sạch hơn
      hẳn, nhưng nó vẽ lại matte chứ không đo đạc, nên luôn kiểm tra mép có khớp ảnh gốc không trước
      khi tin vào mặt nạ.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================================= step 1 -->
  <section class="card p-6 mb-4" aria-labelledby="s1">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-3">
      <span class="chip chip-accent">1</span>
      <h2 id="s1" class="text-lg font-semibold">Upload the render</h2>
      <span class="vi-block-inline text-[0.9rem]" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Tải ảnh lên</span>
    </div>

    <label
      id="drop"
      class="block rounded-xl border-2 border-dashed cursor-pointer text-center py-10 px-4 transition-colors"
      style="border-color: var(--border-strong); background: var(--bg-elevated)"
    >
      <input id="file" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" class="sr-only" />
      <svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--text-faint)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mx-auto mb-3" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 16v2a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2v-2" /><path d="M12 15V3M7 8l5-5 5 5" />
      </svg>
      <p class="font-medium">Drop a JPEG or PNG here, or click to choose</p>
      <p class="vi-block vi-def text-[0.85rem] mt-1" style="border:0;padding:0">
        Kéo thả ảnh JPEG/PNG vào đây, hoặc bấm để chọn file
      </p>
    </label>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================= step 1b: clean logos (optional) -->
  <section id="cleanWrap" class="card mb-4 hidden">
    <details id="cleanDetails">
      <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-baseline gap-2 flex-wrap select-none">
        <span class="chip">1b</span>
        <span class="text-lg font-semibold">Remove a watermark <span class="text-[0.8rem] font-normal" style="color: var(--text-faint)">(optional — open only if the image has text or a logo on it)</span></span>
        <span class="vi-block-inline text-[0.9rem]" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Xoá chữ / logo — chỉ mở nếu ảnh có watermark</span>
        <span class="ml-auto text-[0.85rem]" style="color: var(--accent-cool)">▾</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <ol class="text-[0.9rem] mb-3 grid gap-1" style="color: var(--text-muted); list-style: decimal inside">
          <li>Drag the mouse over the text — a red stroke appears.
            <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Kéo chuột quét lên phần chữ — vệt đỏ hiện ra.</span></li>
          <li>Press <b>Apply</b> — the red area is filled in from its surroundings.
            <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Bấm <b>Apply</b> — vùng đỏ được lấp lại từ nền xung quanh.</span></li>
          <li>Then continue to Segment below.
            <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Rồi bấm Segment ở dưới như bình thường.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-2 text-[0.9rem]">
          <label class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>Brush size</span><span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Cỡ chổi</span>
            <input id="brushSize" type="range" min="6" max="80" value="30" class="accent-[var(--accent)]" />
          </label>
          <button id="applyClean" class="btn btn-primary !py-1.5" type="button">Apply</button>
          <button id="resetClean" class="btn !py-1.5" type="button">Reset</button>
          <button id="dlClean" class="btn !py-1.5 hidden" type="button">Download cleaned image</button>
        </div>
        <p id="cleanMsg" class="text-[0.85rem] mb-3 min-h-[1.2em]" style="color: var(--text-faint)"></p>
        <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--bg)">
          <canvas id="cleanCanvas" class="block w-full h-auto" style="cursor: crosshair; touch-action: none"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================= step 2 -->
  <section id="s2wrap" class="card p-6 mb-4 hidden" aria-labelledby="s2">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-3 flex-wrap">
      <span class="chip chip-accent">2</span>
      <h2 id="s2" class="text-lg font-semibold">Segment</h2>
      <span class="vi-block-inline text-[0.9rem]" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Tách vùng</span>
      <button id="run" class="btn btn-primary ml-auto" type="button">Segment</button>
    </div>

    <!-- engine choice -->
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-4">
      <label class="rounded-lg border p-3 cursor-pointer flex gap-2.5" style="border-color: var(--border-strong)">
        <input type="radio" name="engine" value="local" class="accent-[var(--accent)] mt-1" checked />
        <span class="text-[0.88rem]">
          <b>In-browser</b> — free, and the image never leaves your machine. Geometric
          approximation; edges may need cleanup.
          <span class="vi-block vi-def mt-1 text-[0.84rem]">Chạy trong máy — miễn phí, ảnh không gửi đi đâu. Tách theo hình học, mép có thể cần dặm lại.</span>
        </span>
      </label>
      <label class="rounded-lg border p-3 cursor-pointer flex gap-2.5" style="border-color: var(--border-strong)">
        <input type="radio" name="engine" value="cloud" class="accent-[var(--accent)] mt-1" />
        <span class="text-[0.88rem]">
          <b>Cloud AI matte (Gemini / GPT)</b> — much better object separation, needs your own
          API key. <b>The image is sent to the provider.</b>
          <span class="vi-block vi-def mt-1 text-[0.84rem]">AI đám mây vẽ matte (Gemini hoặc GPT) — tách vật tốt hơn hẳn, cần API key của bạn. <b>Ảnh sẽ được gửi lên nhà cung cấp.</b></span>
        </span>
      </label>
    </div>

    <div id="cloudOpts" class="hidden mb-4 rounded-lg p-3" style="background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border)">
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3 items-end">
        <label class="block">
          <span class="label">Provider</span>
          <select id="provider" class="field !w-auto">
            <option value="gemini">Gemini (~$0.04/image)</option>
            <option value="openai">GPT (~$0.17/image)</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="block">
          <span class="label" id="keyLabel">Google AI API key</span>
          <input id="cloudKey" type="password" class="field" placeholder="AIza…" autocomplete="off" />
        </label>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[0.78rem] mt-1.5" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        <span id="keyHelp">Get one free at aistudio.google.com → Get API key.</span>
        Stored only in this browser (localStorage), never in the site. Do not use a key that
        guards anything important.
        <span class="vi-block-inline">· Key chỉ lưu trong trình duyệt này, không nằm trên site.</span>
      </p>

      <details class="mt-3 rounded-lg" style="border: 1px solid var(--border)">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer select-none px-3 py-2 text-[0.84rem] font-medium">
          No API key? Copy the prompt and paste it into ChatGPT or Gemini yourself
          <span class="vi-block-inline font-normal" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Không có API key? Copy prompt này, dán vào ChatGPT hoặc Gemini kèm ảnh render</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-3 pb-3">
          <p class="text-[0.8rem] mb-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
            Open ChatGPT or the Gemini app, attach your render, paste this prompt, send. It is the
            same prompt this tool uses — the fixed colour schema is inside, so every matte comes
            back with the same colours.
            <span class="vi-block-inline">· Mở ChatGPT hoặc Gemini, đính kèm ảnh render, dán prompt này rồi gửi. Đây chính là prompt tool đang dùng — bảng màu cố định nằm sẵn trong đó, matte nào trả về cũng cùng một bộ màu.</span>
          </p>
          <textarea id="promptText" readonly rows="8" class="field font-mono text-[0.74rem] leading-snug" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-2">
            <button id="copyPrompt" type="button" class="btn !py-1.5 text-[0.84rem]">Copy prompt</button>
            <span id="copyMsg" class="text-[0.8rem]" style="color: var(--success, #4ade80)"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- options (local engine) -->
    <div id="localOpts" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mb-4 text-[0.9rem]">
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer">
        <input id="splitPlanes" type="checkbox" class="accent-[var(--accent)]" checked />
        <span>Split wall planes</span>
        <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Tách mảng tường</span>
      </label>
      <span class="text-[0.8rem]" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        Runs at maximum detail: the full frame plus four overlapping close-up tiles.
        <span class="vi-block-inline">· Chạy ở độ chi tiết tối đa: toàn khung hình cộng 4 ô phóng cận chồng mép.</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <p id="status" class="text-[0.9rem] mb-3" style="color: var(--text-muted)"></p>

    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--bg)">
      <canvas id="preview" class="block w-full h-auto"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div id="controls" class="hidden flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mt-4">
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[0.9rem] cursor-pointer">
        <input id="showOriginal" type="checkbox" class="accent-[var(--accent)]" />
        <span>Check against original</span>
        <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Đối chiếu ảnh gốc</span>
      </label>
      <label id="opWrap" class="hidden items-center gap-2 text-[0.9rem]">
        <span>Opacity</span>
        <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Độ mờ</span>
        <input id="opacity" type="range" min="20" max="100" value="80" class="accent-[var(--accent)]" />
      </label>
    </div>

    <div id="legend" class="hidden mt-4">
      <p class="label !mb-2">Detected <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Nhận diện được</span></p>
      <div id="legendItems" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================= step 2b · SAM click-fix -->
  <section id="samwrap" class="card p-6 mb-4 hidden" aria-labelledby="samh">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-3 flex-wrap">
      <span class="chip chip-accent">2b</span>
      <h2 id="samh" class="text-lg font-semibold">Fix a region by clicking</h2>
      <span class="chip">Beta</span>
      <span class="vi-block-inline text-[0.9rem]" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Sửa vùng bằng cách click</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-[0.86rem] mb-1" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
      When the matte gets an object wrong, click that object on the preview above and a second AI
      (SAM — Segment Anything) traces exactly that object. Click again on missed parts to grow the
      selection; <b>Shift-click</b> marks background to exclude. Then pick the correct colour and
      apply. Tip: tick “Check against original” first so you can see what you are clicking.
    </p>
    <p class="vi-block vi-def text-[0.85rem] mb-3">
      Khi matte nhận sai một vật, click vào vật đó trên ảnh xem trước phía trên — AI thứ hai (SAM —
      Segment Anything) sẽ khoanh đúng vật đó. Click thêm vào phần bị sót để mở rộng vùng chọn;
      <b>Shift-click</b> để loại trừ nền. Rồi chọn đúng màu và áp vào. Mẹo: bật “Đối chiếu ảnh gốc”
      trước để thấy mình đang click vào gì.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <button id="samEnable" class="btn !py-1.5" type="button">Enable click-fix</button>
      <span id="samStatus" class="text-[0.85rem]" style="color: var(--text-muted)"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="samTools" class="hidden flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mt-3">
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[0.88rem]">
        <span>Colour as</span>
        <span class="vi-block-inline" style="color: var(--vi-text)">· Tô màu là</span>
        <select id="samCat" class="field !w-auto !py-1.5"></select>
      </label>
      <button id="samApply" class="btn btn-primary !py-1.5" type="button" disabled>Apply</button>
      <button id="samClear" class="btn !py-1.5" type="button">Clear points</button>
      <button id="samUndo" class="btn !py-1.5 hidden" type="button">Undo</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================= step 3 -->
  <section id="s3wrap" class="card p-6 mb-6 hidden" aria-labelledby="s3">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-3 flex-wrap">
      <span class="chip chip-accent">3</span>
      <h2 id="s3" class="text-lg font-semibold">Save to your computer</h2>
      <span class="vi-block-inline text-[0.9rem]" style="color: var(--vi-text)">Lưu về máy</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-[0.86rem] mb-1" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
      The download is the solid flat-colour label map at the original resolution — drop it into
      Photoshop and select by colour.
    </p>
    <p class="vi-block vi-def text-[0.85rem] mb-4">
      File tải về là bản đồ màu phẳng đặc ở đúng độ phân giải gốc — đưa vào Photoshop rồi chọn theo
      màu. Nên dùng PNG để giữ mép sắc nét.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <button id="dlPng" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Download PNG</button>
      <button id="dlJpg" class="btn" type="button">Download JPEG</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="text-[0.8rem] pb-6" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
    First use downloads the AI model once, then it is cached. Uses your GPU if the browser supports
    WebGPU. Back to <a href={url('/tools')} class="no-underline hover:underline">all tools</a>.
    <span class="vi-block-inline">
      Lần đầu dùng sẽ tải mô hình AI một lần rồi lưu cache. Dùng GPU nếu trình duyệt hỗ trợ WebGPU.
    </span>
  </p>
</Base>

<script>
  const TRANSFORMERS = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@huggingface/transformers@3.8.1';
  const SEG = 'Xenova/segformer-b5-finetuned-ade-640-640';
  const DEPTH = 'onnx-community/depth-anything-v2-small';
  const WORK_MAX = 1440; // post-processing works at this longest side, then upscales

  const VI: Record<string, string> = {
    wall: 'tường', floor: 'sàn', flooring: 'sàn', ceiling: 'trần', windowpane: 'cửa sổ',
    window: 'cửa sổ', door: 'cửa', painting: 'tranh', picture: 'tranh', sofa: 'ghế sofa',
    couch: 'ghế sofa', chair: 'ghế', armchair: 'ghế bành', seat: 'chỗ ngồi', stool: 'ghế đẩu',
    bench: 'ghế băng', ottoman: 'đôn', pouf: 'đôn', table: 'bàn', 'coffee table': 'bàn trà',
    desk: 'bàn làm việc', lamp: 'đèn', light: 'đèn', chandelier: 'đèn chùm', curtain: 'rèm',
    blind: 'rèm sáo', rug: 'thảm', carpet: 'thảm', cushion: 'gối tựa', pillow: 'gối',
    bed: 'giường', cabinet: 'tủ', wardrobe: 'tủ quần áo', 'chest of drawers': 'tủ ngăn kéo',
    sideboard: 'tủ thấp', shelf: 'kệ', bookcase: 'kệ sách', book: 'sách', vase: 'bình',
    bottle: 'chai lọ', plant: 'cây', flower: 'hoa', tree: 'cây', mirror: 'gương',
    television: 'tivi', screen: 'màn hình', fireplace: 'lò sưởi', stairs: 'cầu thang',
    column: 'cột', railing: 'lan can', box: 'hộp', basket: 'giỏ', clock: 'đồng hồ',
    pot: 'chậu', tray: 'khay', countertop: 'mặt bàn bếp', sink: 'bồn rửa', person: 'người',
  };

  const WALL_LIKE = new Set(['wall']);
  const FLOOR_CEIL = new Set(['floor', 'flooring', 'ceiling']);

  /**
   * ADE20K's 150 classes collapse into the groups a compositor actually needs
   * (per the Object-ID matte spec): soft furniture, tables, casegoods, decor,
   * lighting fixtures, plants, and the architectural planes. Each group has a
   * FIXED high-contrast colour, identical on every run, so select-by-colour
   * habits in Photoshop transfer between projects.
   */
  const GROUP: Record<string, string> = {
    sofa: 'soft', couch: 'soft', armchair: 'soft', chair: 'soft', 'swivel chair': 'soft',
    seat: 'soft', cushion: 'soft', pillow: 'soft', ottoman: 'soft', pouf: 'soft',
    bed: 'soft', bench: 'soft',
    table: 'tables', 'coffee table': 'tables', desk: 'tables', stool: 'tables',
    cabinet: 'hard', wardrobe: 'hard', 'chest of drawers': 'hard', sideboard: 'hard',
    shelf: 'hard', bookcase: 'hard', 'kitchen island': 'hard', countertop: 'hard',
    'object at wall': 'hard',
    painting: 'decor', picture: 'decor', poster: 'decor', mirror: 'decor', vase: 'decor',
    bottle: 'decor', book: 'decor', tray: 'decor', box: 'decor', basket: 'decor',
    clock: 'decor', sculpture: 'decor', curtain: 'decor', blind: 'decor',
    television: 'decor', screen: 'decor', monitor: 'decor', fireplace: 'decor',
    plant: 'plant', tree: 'plant', flower: 'plant', grass: 'floor',
    lamp: 'lighting', chandelier: 'lighting', light: 'lighting', sconce: 'lighting',
    floor: 'floor', flooring: 'floor', earth: 'floor', ceiling: 'ceiling',
    rug: 'rug', carpet: 'rug',
    door: 'door', 'double door': 'door', windowpane: 'window', window: 'window',
    stairs: 'arch', stairway: 'arch', column: 'arch', railing: 'arch',
  };

  const GROUP_COLOR: Record<string, [number, number, number]> = {
    'wall|0': [0, 128, 153],   // left wall — deep teal
    'wall|1': [128, 0, 128],   // centre wall — purple
    'wall|2': [192, 0, 128],   // right wall — magenta
    ceiling: [128, 0, 0],      // dark red
    floor: [0, 0, 128],        // navy
    rug: [176, 48, 96],        // maroon-pink, per the carpet-is-separate rule
    soft: [0, 128, 64],        // emerald
    tables: [64, 224, 208],    // turquoise
    hard: [255, 215, 0],       // gold — consoles, cabinets, shelves
    decor: [106, 90, 205],     // slate blue — artwork & decor
    lighting: [255, 255, 255], // pure white — track lights, strips, lamps
    plant: [50, 205, 50],      // lime
    door: [255, 128, 0],       // orange
    window: [0, 191, 255],     // sky blue
    arch: [192, 192, 192],     // silver — stairs, columns, railings
  };
  const isArch = (n?: string) => !!n && (WALL_LIKE.has(first(n)) || FLOOR_CEIL.has(first(n)));
  const first = (label: string) => label.toLowerCase().split(';')[0].trim();

  const $ = <T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as T | null;
  const fileInput = $<HTMLInputElement>('file');
  const drop = $('drop');
  const runBtn = $<HTMLButtonElement>('run');
  const statusEl = $('status');
  const preview = $<HTMLCanvasElement>('preview');

  let sourceImage: HTMLImageElement | null = null;
  let labelCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null = null; // solid label map, full res
  let segmenter: any = null, depther: any = null;

  const setStatus = (m: string, tone = 'var(--text-muted)') => {
    if (statusEl) { statusEl.textContent = m; statusEl.style.color = tone; }
  };

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- upload
  let originalImage: HTMLImageElement | null = null; // pristine upload, for Reset
  let cleanMask: Uint8Array | null = null; // 1 = brushed for removal

  function handleFile(file: File) {
    if (!file || !file.type.startsWith('image/')) return;
    const img = new Image();
    img.onload = () => {
      originalImage = img;
      sourceImage = img;
      cleanMask = new Uint8Array(img.naturalWidth * img.naturalHeight);
      labelCanvas = null;
      resetSam(true);
      $('cleanWrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
      $('dlClean')?.classList.add('hidden');
      $('s2wrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
      $('s3wrap')?.classList.add('hidden');
      $('samwrap')?.classList.add('hidden');
      $('controls')?.classList.add('hidden');
      $('legend')?.classList.add('hidden');
      drawClean();
      drawPreview();
      setStatus('Ready — press Segment. · Sẵn sàng — bấm Segment.');
      $('cleanWrap')?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
    };
    img.src = URL.createObjectURL(file);
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------- clean text/logo (step 1b)
  const cleanCanvas = $<HTMLCanvasElement>('cleanCanvas');

  function drawClean() {
    if (!cleanCanvas || !sourceImage) return;
    const W = sourceImage.naturalWidth, H = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    cleanCanvas.width = W; cleanCanvas.height = H;
    const ctx = cleanCanvas.getContext('2d')!;
    ctx.drawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0);
    if (!cleanMask) return;
    // show the brushed area as a red tint
    const id = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H);
    for (let i = 0; i < W * H; i++) if (cleanMask[i]) {
      id.data[i * 4] = Math.min(255, id.data[i * 4] * 0.4 + 200);
      id.data[i * 4 + 1] *= 0.35; id.data[i * 4 + 2] *= 0.35;
    }
    ctx.putImageData(id, 0, 0);
  }

  let painting = false;
  function stamp(ev: PointerEvent) {
    if (!cleanCanvas || !cleanMask || !sourceImage) return;
    const rect = cleanCanvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    const W = sourceImage.naturalWidth, H = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    const x = ((ev.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * W;
    const y = ((ev.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * H;
    const r = Number(($<HTMLInputElement>('brushSize'))?.value ?? 24) * (W / rect.width) * 0.5;
    const r2 = r * r;
    const x0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor(x - r)), x1 = Math.min(W - 1, Math.ceil(x + r));
    const y0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor(y - r)), y1 = Math.min(H - 1, Math.ceil(y + r));
    for (let yy = y0; yy <= y1; yy++) for (let xx = x0; xx <= x1; xx++) {
      const dx = xx - x, dy = yy - y;
      if (dx * dx + dy * dy <= r2) cleanMask[yy * W + xx] = 1;
    }
    drawClean();
  }
  cleanCanvas?.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    painting = true;
    try { cleanCanvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {}
    stamp(e);
  });
  cleanCanvas?.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (painting) stamp(e); });
  cleanCanvas?.addEventListener('pointerup', () => { painting = false; });

  /**
   * Diffusion inpaint: solve the hole at quarter resolution (Jacobi iterations
   * over masked pixels), paste back bilinearly, then a few full-res passes to
   * blend the seam. Harmonic fill — smooth and natural on flat surfaces, which
   * is where watermarks live.
   */
  function inpaint(img: HTMLImageElement, mask: Uint8Array): HTMLCanvasElement {
    const W = img.naturalWidth, H = img.naturalHeight;
    const full = document.createElement('canvas');
    full.width = W; full.height = H;
    const fctx = full.getContext('2d')!;
    fctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0);
    const fid = fctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H);

    // quarter-res working copy
    const s = 4, w = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(W / s)), h = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(H / s));
    const rgb = new Float32Array(w * h * 3);
    const hole = new Uint8Array(w * h);
    const cntArr = new Int32Array(w * h);
    for (let Y = 0; Y < H; Y++) for (let X = 0; X < W; X++) {
      const q = ((Y / s) | 0) * w + ((X / s) | 0), p = (Y * W + X) * 4;
      if (mask[Y * W + X]) { hole[q] = 1; continue; } // masked px must NOT seed the average
      rgb[q * 3] += fid.data[p]; rgb[q * 3 + 1] += fid.data[p + 1]; rgb[q * 3 + 2] += fid.data[p + 2];
      cntArr[q]++;
    }
    for (let q = 0; q < w * h; q++) { const n = cntArr[q]; if (n) { rgb[q * 3] /= n; rgb[q * 3 + 1] /= n; rgb[q * 3 + 2] /= n; } }
    // cells with no clean pixels: flood-fill initial values from known neighbours
    let pending = true;
    while (pending) {
      pending = false;
      for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) {
        const q = y * w + x; if (cntArr[q]) continue;
        let r = 0, g = 0, b = 0, n = 0;
        const add = (j: number) => { if (cntArr[j]) { r += rgb[j * 3]; g += rgb[j * 3 + 1]; b += rgb[j * 3 + 2]; n++; } };
        if (x > 0) add(q - 1); if (x < w - 1) add(q + 1); if (y > 0) add(q - w); if (y < h - 1) add(q + w);
        if (n) { rgb[q * 3] = r / n; rgb[q * 3 + 1] = g / n; rgb[q * 3 + 2] = b / n; cntArr[q] = -1; }
        else pending = true;
      }
      // -1 markers become known for the next sweep
      for (let q = 0; q < w * h; q++) if (cntArr[q] === -1) cntArr[q] = 1;
    }

    // Jacobi diffusion on hole pixels
    for (let it = 0; it < 300; it++) {
      for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) {
        const q = y * w + x; if (!hole[q]) continue;
        let r = 0, g = 0, b = 0, n = 0;
        const add = (j: number) => { r += rgb[j * 3]; g += rgb[j * 3 + 1]; b += rgb[j * 3 + 2]; n++; };
        if (x > 0) add(q - 1); if (x < w - 1) add(q + 1);
        if (y > 0) add(q - w); if (y < h - 1) add(q + w);
        if (n) { rgb[q * 3] = r / n; rgb[q * 3 + 1] = g / n; rgb[q * 3 + 2] = b / n; }
      }
    }

    // paste back into hole pixels, bilinear from the quarter grid
    for (let Y = 0; Y < H; Y++) for (let X = 0; X < W; X++) {
      if (!mask[Y * W + X]) continue;
      const fx = Math.min(w - 1.001, X / s), fy = Math.min(h - 1.001, Y / s);
      const x0 = fx | 0, y0 = fy | 0, tx = fx - x0, ty = fy - y0;
      const p = (Y * W + X) * 4;
      for (let ch = 0; ch < 3; ch++) {
        const a = rgb[(y0 * w + x0) * 3 + ch], b2 = rgb[(y0 * w + x0 + 1) * 3 + ch];
        const c2 = rgb[((y0 + 1) * w + x0) * 3 + ch], d2 = rgb[((y0 + 1) * w + x0 + 1) * 3 + ch];
        fid.data[p + ch] = a * (1 - tx) * (1 - ty) + b2 * tx * (1 - ty) + c2 * (1 - tx) * ty + d2 * tx * ty;
      }
    }
    // blend seams: a few full-res passes over masked px
    const D = fid.data;
    for (let it = 0; it < 6; it++) {
      for (let Y = 1; Y < H - 1; Y++) for (let X = 1; X < W - 1; X++) {
        const i = Y * W + X; if (!mask[i]) continue;
        const p = i * 4;
        for (let ch = 0; ch < 3; ch++)
          D[p + ch] = (D[p - 4 + ch] + D[p + 4 + ch] + D[p - W * 4 + ch] + D[p + W * 4 + ch]) / 4;
      }
    }
    fctx.putImageData(fid, 0, 0);
    return full;
  }

  const setCleanMsg = (m: string, tone = 'var(--text-faint)') => {
    const el = $('cleanMsg'); if (el) { el.textContent = m; el.style.color = tone; }
  };

  $('applyClean')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!originalImage || !cleanMask) return;
    let any = false; for (let i = 0; i < cleanMask.length; i++) if (cleanMask[i]) { any = true; break; }
    if (!any) {
      // The button must never look dead — the earlier silent return read as broken.
      setCleanMsg('Brush over the text first — drag the mouse on the image below. · Hãy quét chổi lên phần chữ trước — kéo chuột trên ảnh bên dưới.', 'var(--warning)');
      return;
    }
    setCleanMsg('Filling… · Đang lấp vùng đã quét…');
    setTimeout(() => {
      const cleaned = inpaint(sourceImage!, cleanMask!);
      const img = new Image();
      img.onload = () => {
        sourceImage = img;
        cleanMask = new Uint8Array(img.naturalWidth * img.naturalHeight);
        labelCanvas = null;
        resetSam(true);
        $('dlClean')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        drawClean(); drawPreview();
        setCleanMsg('Done — brush more, or scroll down and press Segment. · Đã lấp xong — quét tiếp, hoặc kéo xuống bấm Segment.', 'var(--success)');
      };
      img.src = cleaned.toDataURL('image/png');
    }, 30);
  });

  $('resetClean')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!originalImage) return;
    sourceImage = originalImage;
    cleanMask = new Uint8Array(originalImage.naturalWidth * originalImage.naturalHeight);
    labelCanvas = null;
    resetSam(true);
    $('dlClean')?.classList.add('hidden');
    drawClean(); drawPreview();
    setCleanMsg('Back to the original image. · Đã trả về ảnh gốc.');
  });

  $('dlClean')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!sourceImage) return;
    const c = canvasOfImage(sourceImage);
    c.toBlob((b) => {
      if (!b) return;
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = URL.createObjectURL(b); a.download = 'cleaned.png'; a.click();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href);
    }, 'image/png');
  });
  fileInput?.addEventListener('change', () => { if (fileInput.files?.[0]) handleFile(fileInput.files[0]); });
  ['dragover', 'dragenter'].forEach((ev) => drop?.addEventListener(ev, (e) => { e.preventDefault(); (drop as HTMLElement).style.borderColor = 'var(--accent)'; }));
  ['dragleave', 'drop'].forEach((ev) => drop?.addEventListener(ev, (e) => { e.preventDefault(); (drop as HTMLElement).style.borderColor = 'var(--border-strong)'; }));
  drop?.addEventListener('drop', (e) => { const f = (e as DragEvent).dataTransfer?.files?.[0]; if (f) handleFile(f); });

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- preview
  function drawPreview() {
    if (!preview || !sourceImage) return;
    const W = sourceImage.naturalWidth, H = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    preview.width = W; preview.height = H;
    const ctx = preview.getContext('2d')!;
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    const showOrig = ($<HTMLInputElement>('showOriginal'))?.checked;
    const alpha = (Number(($<HTMLInputElement>('opacity'))?.value ?? 80)) / 100;

    if (!labelCanvas) { ctx.drawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0); return; }
    if (showOrig) {
      ctx.drawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0);
      ctx.globalAlpha = alpha;
      ctx.drawImage(labelCanvas, 0, 0);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    } else {
      ctx.drawImage(labelCanvas, 0, 0); // solid labels by default
    }
    // SAM click-fix overlay: the traced object + the points she placed
    if (samActive && samMaskCanvas) {
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.45;
      ctx.drawImage(samMaskCanvas, 0, 0, W, H);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }
    if (samActive && samPoints.length) {
      const r = Math.max(4, W / 220);
      for (const p of samPoints) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fillStyle = p.label ? '#22c55e' : '#ef4444';
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(1.5, r / 3);
        ctx.strokeStyle = '#fff';
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
  }
  $('showOriginal')?.addEventListener('change', () => {
    $('opWrap')?.classList.toggle('hidden', !($<HTMLInputElement>('showOriginal'))?.checked);
    $('opWrap')?.classList.toggle('flex', !!($<HTMLInputElement>('showOriginal'))?.checked);
    drawPreview();
  });
  $('opacity')?.addEventListener('input', drawPreview);

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- models
  async function getSegmenter(onProgress: any) {
    if (segmenter) return segmenter;
    const { pipeline } = await import(/* @vite-ignore */ TRANSFORMERS);
    const device = (navigator as any).gpu ? 'webgpu' : 'wasm';
    try { segmenter = await pipeline('image-segmentation', SEG, { device, progress_callback: onProgress }); }
    catch { segmenter = await pipeline('image-segmentation', SEG, { device: 'wasm', progress_callback: onProgress }); }
    return segmenter;
  }
  /** GPU inference can die mid-run (device lost, out of GPU memory on a big
   *  image) even after loading fine — rebuild the pipeline on the CPU path. */
  async function rebuildSegmenterOnWasm(onProgress: any) {
    const { pipeline } = await import(/* @vite-ignore */ TRANSFORMERS);
    segmenter = await pipeline('image-segmentation', SEG, { device: 'wasm', progress_callback: onProgress });
    return segmenter;
  }
  async function getDepther(onProgress: any) {
    if (depther) return depther;
    const { pipeline } = await import(/* @vite-ignore */ TRANSFORMERS);
    const device = (navigator as any).gpu ? 'webgpu' : 'wasm';
    try { depther = await pipeline('depth-estimation', DEPTH, { device, progress_callback: onProgress }); }
    catch { depther = await pipeline('depth-estimation', DEPTH, { device: 'wasm', progress_callback: onProgress }); }
    return depther;
  }

  // --------------------------------------------- SAM click-fix (step 2b)
  // A second, promptable model: she clicks the object the matte got wrong,
  // SlimSAM traces exactly that object, and the mask is painted into the
  // matte with the schema colour she picks. The image is encoded once
  // (get_image_embeddings); each click only runs the tiny mask decoder.
  const SAM = 'Xenova/slimsam-77-uniform';
  let samKit: { model: any; processor: any; Tensor: any; RawImage: any } | null = null;
  let samEmb: any = null, samEmbInputs: any = null;
  let samActive = false, samBusy = false;
  let samPoints: Array<{ x: number; y: number; label: number }> = [];
  let samMask: Uint8Array | null = null;
  let samMaskCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null = null;
  const samUndo: ImageData[] = [];

  function setSamStatus(t: string, color = 'var(--text-muted)') {
    const el = $('samStatus');
    if (el) { el.textContent = t; el.style.color = color; }
  }
  function resetSam(dropEmbeddings: boolean) {
    samPoints = []; samMask = null; samMaskCanvas = null;
    const ap = $<HTMLButtonElement>('samApply'); if (ap) ap.disabled = true;
    if (dropEmbeddings) {
      samEmb = null; samEmbInputs = null;
      samUndo.length = 0; $('samUndo')?.classList.add('hidden');
    }
    if (samActive) drawPreview();
  }

  async function getSamKit() {
    if (samKit) return samKit;
    const T: any = await import(/* @vite-ignore */ TRANSFORMERS);
    const prog = (p: any) => {
      if (p.status === 'progress' && p.file?.endsWith?.('.onnx'))
        setSamStatus(`Loading SAM model… ${Math.round(p.progress ?? 0)}% · Đang tải mô hình SAM…`);
    };
    const processor = await T.AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(SAM, {});
    let model;
    try {
      model = await T.SamModel.from_pretrained(SAM, {
        device: (navigator as any).gpu ? 'webgpu' : 'wasm',
        dtype: (navigator as any).gpu ? 'fp16' : 'q8',
        progress_callback: prog,
      });
    } catch {
      model = await T.SamModel.from_pretrained(SAM, { device: 'wasm', dtype: 'q8', progress_callback: prog });
    }
    samKit = { model, processor, Tensor: T.Tensor, RawImage: T.RawImage };
    return samKit;
  }

  async function ensureSamEmbeddings() {
    if (samEmb || !sourceImage) return;
    const kit = await getSamKit();
    setSamStatus('Reading the image once — a few seconds… · Đang đọc ảnh một lần — vài giây…');
    const W = sourceImage.naturalWidth, H = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    const c = document.createElement('canvas');
    c.width = W; c.height = H;
    const cctx = c.getContext('2d')!;
    cctx.drawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0);
    const raw = new kit.RawImage(cctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data, W, H, 4);
    samEmbInputs = await kit.processor(raw);
    samEmb = await kit.model.get_image_embeddings(samEmbInputs);
  }

  async function updateSamMask() {
    if (!samPoints.length || !sourceImage) return;
    const kit = await getSamKit();
    await ensureSamEmbeddings();
    const origW = sourceImage.naturalWidth, origH = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    const reshaped = samEmbInputs.reshaped_input_sizes[0]; // [h, w]
    const n = samPoints.length;
    const pts = new Float32Array(n * 2);
    const lbl = new BigInt64Array(n);
    samPoints.forEach((p, i) => {
      pts[i * 2] = (p.x / origW) * reshaped[1];
      pts[i * 2 + 1] = (p.y / origH) * reshaped[0];
      lbl[i] = BigInt(p.label);
    });
    const input_points = new kit.Tensor('float32', pts, [1, 1, n, 2]);
    const input_labels = new kit.Tensor('int64', lbl, [1, 1, n]);
    const out = await kit.model({ ...samEmb, input_points, input_labels });
    const masks = await kit.processor.post_process_masks(out.pred_masks, samEmbInputs.original_sizes, samEmbInputs.reshaped_input_sizes);
    const scores = out.iou_scores.data as Float32Array | number[];
    let best = 0;
    for (let i = 1; i < scores.length; i++) if (scores[i] > scores[best]) best = i;
    const m = masks[0]; // [1, 3, H, W]
    const dims = m.dims, mh = dims[dims.length - 2], mw = dims[dims.length - 1];
    const data = m.data;
    const off = best * mh * mw;
    samMask = new Uint8Array(mh * mw);
    for (let i = 0; i < mh * mw; i++) samMask[i] = data[off + i] ? 1 : 0;
    // highlight canvas the preview blends on top
    samMaskCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    samMaskCanvas.width = mw; samMaskCanvas.height = mh;
    const hctx = samMaskCanvas.getContext('2d')!;
    const hd = hctx.createImageData(mw, mh);
    for (let i = 0; i < mh * mw; i++) if (samMask[i]) {
      hd.data[i * 4] = 255; hd.data[i * 4 + 1] = 255; hd.data[i * 4 + 2] = 255; hd.data[i * 4 + 3] = 255;
    }
    hctx.putImageData(hd, 0, 0);
    const ap = $<HTMLButtonElement>('samApply'); if (ap) ap.disabled = false;
  }

  $('samEnable')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const btn = $<HTMLButtonElement>('samEnable')!;
    if (samActive) {
      samActive = false;
      btn.textContent = 'Enable click-fix';
      $('samTools')?.classList.add('hidden'); $('samTools')?.classList.remove('flex');
      if (preview) preview.style.cursor = '';
      setSamStatus('');
      resetSam(false);
      drawPreview();
      return;
    }
    samActive = true;
    btn.textContent = 'Disable click-fix';
    // schema colours she can paint with
    const sel = $<HTMLSelectElement>('samCat');
    if (sel && !sel.options.length) {
      for (const [key, [en, vi]] of Object.entries(KEY_LABELS)) {
        const o = document.createElement('option');
        o.value = key; o.textContent = `${en} · ${vi}`;
        sel.appendChild(o);
      }
    }
    $('samTools')?.classList.remove('hidden'); $('samTools')?.classList.add('flex');
    if (preview) preview.style.cursor = 'crosshair';
    try {
      await getSamKit();
      await ensureSamEmbeddings();
      setSamStatus('Ready — click an object on the preview. · Sẵn sàng — click vào một vật trên ảnh xem trước.', 'var(--success)');
    } catch (e: any) {
      samActive = false;
      btn.textContent = 'Enable click-fix';
      if (preview) preview.style.cursor = '';
      setSamStatus(`Could not load SAM: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 90)} · Không tải được SAM — thử lại hoặc tải lại trang.`, 'var(--warning)');
    }
  });

  preview?.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
    if (!samActive || samBusy || !labelCanvas || !sourceImage) return;
    const rect = preview.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (!rect.width || !rect.height) return;
    const x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * sourceImage.naturalWidth;
    const y = ((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * sourceImage.naturalHeight;
    samPoints.push({ x, y, label: (e as MouseEvent).shiftKey ? 0 : 1 });
    samBusy = true;
    setSamStatus('Tracing… · Đang khoanh vùng…');
    try {
      await updateSamMask();
      setSamStatus('Good? Pick a colour and Apply — or keep clicking to refine. · Ổn chưa? Chọn màu rồi Apply — hoặc click tiếp để chỉnh.', 'var(--success)');
    } catch (err: any) {
      samPoints.pop();
      setSamStatus(`SAM failed: ${String(err?.message ?? err).slice(0, 90)}`, 'var(--warning)');
    }
    samBusy = false;
    drawPreview();
  });

  $('samClear')?.addEventListener('click', () => { resetSam(false); setSamStatus('Points cleared. · Đã xoá điểm.'); });

  $('samApply')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!samMask || !labelCanvas) return;
    const key = ($<HTMLSelectElement>('samCat'))?.value ?? 'decor';
    const col = GROUP_COLOR[key] ?? [106, 90, 205];
    const W = labelCanvas.width, H = labelCanvas.height;
    const lctx = labelCanvas.getContext('2d')!;
    // snapshot for undo (cap the stack — full-res frames are heavy)
    samUndo.push(lctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H));
    if (samUndo.length > 3) samUndo.shift();
    $('samUndo')?.classList.remove('hidden');
    const img = lctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H);
    for (let i = 0; i < W * H; i++) if (samMask[i]) {
      img.data[i * 4] = col[0]; img.data[i * 4 + 1] = col[1]; img.data[i * 4 + 2] = col[2];
    }
    lctx.putImageData(img, 0, 0);
    resetSam(false);
    setSamStatus('Applied. Click the next object, or download below. · Đã áp màu. Click vật tiếp theo, hoặc tải về ở dưới.', 'var(--success)');
    drawPreview();
  });

  $('samUndo')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const snap = samUndo.pop();
    if (!snap || !labelCanvas) return;
    labelCanvas.getContext('2d')!.putImageData(snap, 0, 0);
    if (!samUndo.length) $('samUndo')?.classList.add('hidden');
    resetSam(false);
    setSamStatus('Undone. · Đã hoàn tác.');
    drawPreview();
  });

  // ---------------------------------------------- cloud engine (Gemini)
  const GEMINI_MODEL = 'gemini-2.5-flash-image';
  const KEY_STORE = 'pastelux-gemini-key';

  // The prompt is her Object-ID matte spec, pinned to OUR fixed colour schema
  // so both engines produce the same legend.
  const MATTE_PROMPT = `Convert this architectural render into an Object ID matte pass (segmentation map), like a V-Ray WireColor render element.

STRICT RULES:
1. Output ONLY the matte image. Same aspect ratio and framing as the input. No legend, no text, no border.
2. 100% solid flat colours. No gradients, no shading, no shadows, no anti-aliasing bleed. Razor-sharp boundaries that follow the exact geometry of the input.
3. Colour purely by object identity, never by lighting. One continuous object = one uniform colour across its whole surface.
4. Separate wall planes by orientation. Detect every small and distant object: track lights, recessed spotlights, LED strips, consoles under artwork, tabletop decor.
5. Remove any watermark, logo or text; fill that area as its background surface.

FIXED COLOUR SCHEMA (use these exact colours):
- Left wall plane #008099, centre/back wall plane #800080, right wall plane #C00080
- Ceiling #800000, floor #000080, rug/carpet #B03060
- Sofas, armchairs, cushions, beds #008040
- Coffee/side/dining tables, desks #40E0D0
- Cabinets, consoles, shelves, counters #FFD700
- Artwork, mirrors, decor objects #6A5ACD
- ALL lighting fixtures (track lights, spots, pendants, lamps, LED strips) #FFFFFF
- Plants #32CD32, doors #FF8000, windows #00BFFF, stairs/columns #C0C0C0
Distinct objects of the same category may share the category colour.`;

  const engineRadios = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="engine"]')];
  const currentEngine = () => engineRadios.find((r) => r.checked)?.value ?? 'local';
  const keyInput = $<HTMLInputElement>('cloudKey');
  const providerSel = $<HTMLSelectElement>('provider');
  const currentProvider = () => providerSel?.value ?? 'gemini';
  const keyStoreFor = (prov: string) => (prov === 'openai' ? 'pastelux-openai-key' : KEY_STORE);

  const PROVIDER_UI: Record<string, { label: string; placeholder: string; help: string }> = {
    gemini: { label: 'Google AI API key', placeholder: 'AIza…', help: 'Get one free at aistudio.google.com → Get API key.' },
    openai: { label: 'OpenAI API key', placeholder: 'sk-…', help: 'Create one at platform.openai.com → API keys. gpt-image-1 may require a verified organisation.' },
  };
  function syncProviderUI() {
    const ui = PROVIDER_UI[currentProvider()];
    const lb = $('keyLabel'), hp = $('keyHelp');
    if (lb) lb.textContent = ui.label;
    if (hp) hp.textContent = ui.help + ' ';
    if (keyInput) {
      keyInput.placeholder = ui.placeholder;
      try { keyInput.value = localStorage.getItem(keyStoreFor(currentProvider())) ?? ''; } catch {}
    }
  }
  providerSel?.addEventListener('change', syncProviderUI);
  syncProviderUI();

  // copy-paste path for using ChatGPT / Gemini apps directly, no API key
  const promptText = $<HTMLTextAreaElement>('promptText');
  if (promptText) promptText.value = MATTE_PROMPT;
  $('copyPrompt')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const msg = $('copyMsg');
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(MATTE_PROMPT);
    } catch {
      promptText?.select();
      document.execCommand('copy');
    }
    if (msg) {
      msg.textContent = 'Copied ✓ · Đã copy';
      setTimeout(() => { msg.textContent = ''; }, 2500);
    }
  });

  engineRadios.forEach((r) =>
    r.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const cloud = currentEngine() === 'cloud';
      $('cloudOpts')?.classList.toggle('hidden', !cloud);
      $('localOpts')?.classList.toggle('hidden', cloud);
    })
  );

  /** Decode a base64 matte, upscale nearest to native res, show the schema legend. */
  async function applyMatte(data: string, mime: string) {
    const origW = sourceImage!.naturalWidth, origH = sourceImage!.naturalHeight;
    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
      const img = new Image();
      img.onload = () => {
        labelCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
        labelCanvas.width = origW; labelCanvas.height = origH;
        const lctx = labelCanvas.getContext('2d')!;
        lctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
        lctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, origW, origH);
        resolve();
      };
      img.onerror = () => reject(new Error('Could not decode the returned image'));
      img.src = `data:${mime};base64,${data}`;
    });
    const legendMap = new Map<string, { color: [number, number, number]; regions: number; area: number }>();
    let order = 0;
    for (const k of ['wall|0', 'wall|1', 'wall|2', 'ceiling', 'floor', 'rug', 'soft', 'tables', 'hard', 'decor', 'lighting', 'plant', 'door', 'window']) {
      legendMap.set(k, { color: GROUP_COLOR[k], regions: 1, area: 1000 - order++ });
    }
    renderLegend(legendMap);
  }

  async function runCloud(): Promise<boolean> {
    const prov = currentProvider();
    const key = keyInput?.value.trim();
    if (!key) {
      setStatus(
        prov === 'openai'
          ? 'Paste your OpenAI API key first (platform.openai.com → API keys). · Hãy dán API key OpenAI trước.'
          : 'Paste your Google AI API key first (aistudio.google.com → Get API key). · Hãy dán API key Google trước.',
        'var(--warning)'
      );
      return false;
    }
    try { localStorage.setItem(keyStoreFor(prov), key); } catch {}

    const origW = sourceImage!.naturalWidth, origH = sourceImage!.naturalHeight;
    // cap the upload; the models work around 1k anyway
    const inScale = Math.min(1, 1536 / Math.max(origW, origH));
    const c = document.createElement('canvas');
    c.width = Math.round(origW * inScale); c.height = Math.round(origH * inScale);
    c.getContext('2d')!.drawImage(sourceImage!, 0, 0, c.width, c.height);

    if (prov === 'openai') {
      setStatus('Sending to GPT — often 30–90s… · Đang gửi lên GPT — thường mất 30–90 giây…');
      const blob: Blob = await new Promise((r) => c.toBlob((b) => r(b!), 'image/png'));
      const form = new FormData();
      form.append('model', 'gpt-image-1');
      form.append('image', blob, 'render.png');
      form.append('prompt', MATTE_PROMPT);
      form.append('size', 'auto');
      form.append('n', '1');
      const res = await fetch('https://api.openai.com/v1/images/edits', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },
        body: form,
      });
      if (!res.ok) {
        const body = await res.text().catch(() => '');
        const msg = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(body)?.error?.message ?? body; } catch { return body; } })();
        throw new Error(`GPT ${res.status}: ${String(msg).slice(0, 140)}`);
      }
      const json = await res.json();
      const b64out = json?.data?.[0]?.b64_json;
      if (!b64out) throw new Error('GPT returned no image');
      await applyMatte(b64out, 'image/png');
      return true;
    }

    const b64 = c.toDataURL('image/jpeg', 0.92).split(',')[1];
    setStatus('Sending to Gemini — usually 10–30s… · Đang gửi lên Gemini — thường mất 10–30 giây…');
    const res = await fetch(
      `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/${GEMINI_MODEL}:generateContent?key=${encodeURIComponent(key)}`,
      {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          contents: [{ role: 'user', parts: [
            { inline_data: { mime_type: 'image/jpeg', data: b64 } },
            { text: MATTE_PROMPT },
          ] }],
          generationConfig: { responseModalities: ['TEXT', 'IMAGE'] },
        }),
      }
    );
    if (!res.ok) {
      const body = await res.text().catch(() => '');
      const msg = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(body)?.error?.message ?? body; } catch { return body; } })();
      throw new Error(`Gemini ${res.status}: ${String(msg).slice(0, 140)}`);
    }
    const json = await res.json();
    const parts = json?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts ?? [];
    const imgPart = parts.find((p: any) => p.inlineData?.data || p.inline_data?.data);
    if (!imgPart) {
      const textPart = parts.find((p: any) => p.text)?.text?.slice(0, 120);
      throw new Error(textPart ? `Model returned text instead of an image: ${textPart}` : 'Model returned no image');
    }
    const data = imgPart.inlineData?.data ?? imgPart.inline_data?.data;
    const mime = imgPart.inlineData?.mimeType ?? imgPart.inline_data?.mime_type ?? 'image/png';
    await applyMatte(data, mime);
    return true;
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- run
  runBtn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!sourceImage) return;
    runBtn.disabled = true;
    const t0 = performance.now();
    const wantPlanes = ($<HTMLInputElement>('splitPlanes'))?.checked ?? true;

    const onProgress = (p: any) => {
      if (p?.status === 'progress' && p.total) {
        const pct = Math.round((p.loaded / p.total) * 100);
        setStatus(`Downloading model… ${pct}% · Đang tải mô hình… ${pct}%`);
      }
    };

    try {
      if (currentEngine() === 'cloud') {
        const ok = await runCloud();
        if (!ok) { runBtn.disabled = false; return; } // status already explains why
        drawPreview();
        $('controls')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        $('legend')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        $('s3wrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        $('samwrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        const csecs = ((performance.now() - t0) / 1000).toFixed(1);
        setStatus(`Done in ${csecs}s — check alignment with the overlay before trusting edges. · Xong sau ${csecs}s — bật "Đối chiếu ảnh gốc" kiểm tra độ khớp trước khi dùng.`, 'var(--success)');
        runBtn.disabled = false;
        return;
      }
      setStatus('Loading models… · Đang tải mô hình…');
      let seg = await getSegmenter(onProgress);
      const dep = wantPlanes ? await getDepther(onProgress) : null;

      // work-grid dimensions (shared by inference merge and post-processing)
      const origW = sourceImage.naturalWidth, origH = sourceImage.naturalHeight;
      const scale = Math.min(1, WORK_MAX / Math.max(origW, origH));
      const W = Math.max(16, Math.round(origW * scale));
      const H = Math.max(16, Math.round(origH * scale));

      /**
       * Tiled inference. The model only ever sees ~640px, so a small or
       * distant object is a handful of pixels to it. One pass over the whole
       * frame anchors the big surfaces; four overlapping tiles each give the
       * model a close-up where small objects are ~2x larger. Masks merge by
       * label with a per-pixel max.
       */
      const src = canvasOfImage(sourceImage);
      const tiles: Array<{ sx: number; sy: number; sw: number; sh: number }> = [
        { sx: 0, sy: 0, sw: origW, sh: origH },
      ];
      const tw = Math.ceil(origW * 0.6), th = Math.ceil(origH * 0.6);
      for (const [tx, ty] of [[0, 0], [origW - tw, 0], [0, origH - th], [origW - tw, origH - th]] as const)
        tiles.push({ sx: tx, sy: ty, sw: tw, sh: th });

      const grids = new Map<string, Uint8Array>();
      let depOut: any = null;
      for (let i = 0; i < tiles.length; i++) {
        const t = tiles[i];
        setStatus(`Analysing ${i + 1}/${tiles.length}… · Đang phân tích ${i + 1}/${tiles.length}…`);
        // The model resizes everything to ~640px internally, so feeding it a
        // 4000px tile is pure memory cost with zero quality gain. Cap the
        // input and use JPEG — the encode is far cheaper than PNG.
        const inScale = Math.min(1, 1280 / Math.max(t.sw, t.sh));
        const tc = document.createElement('canvas');
        tc.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(t.sw * inScale));
        tc.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(t.sh * inScale));
        tc.getContext('2d')!.drawImage(src, t.sx, t.sy, t.sw, t.sh, 0, 0, tc.width, tc.height);
        const url = tc.toDataURL('image/jpeg', 0.92);

        let segOut: any = null, maybeDep: any = null;
        try {
          const jobs: Promise<any>[] = [seg(url)];
          if (i === 0 && dep) jobs.push(dep(url)); // depth only needs the full frame
          [segOut, maybeDep] = await Promise.all(jobs);
        } catch (tileErr: any) {
          console.error(`pass ${i + 1} failed`, tileErr);
          if (i === 0) {
            // The anchor pass must succeed — retry it on the CPU path.
            setStatus('GPU failed, retrying on CPU (slower)… · GPU lỗi, thử lại bằng CPU (chậm hơn)…', 'var(--warning)');
            seg = await rebuildSegmenterOnWasm(onProgress);
            segOut = await seg(url);
            if (dep) { try { maybeDep = await dep(url); } catch { maybeDep = null; } }
          } else {
            // A close-up tile is an enhancement; losing one must not kill the run.
            continue;
          }
        }
        if (maybeDep) depOut = maybeDep;
        if (!Array.isArray(segOut)) continue;

        // tile rect in work-grid coordinates
        const gx = Math.round((t.sx / origW) * W), gy = Math.round((t.sy / origH) * H);
        const gw = Math.max(1, Math.round((t.sw / origW) * W)), gh = Math.max(1, Math.round((t.sh / origH) * H));
        for (const s of segOut) {
          const m = channelToGrid(s.mask, gw, gh, false);
          let g = grids.get(s.label);
          if (!g) { g = new Uint8Array(W * H); grids.set(s.label, g); }
          for (let y = 0; y < gh; y++) {
            const ry = gy + y; if (ry >= H) break;
            for (let x = 0; x < gw; x++) {
              const rx = gx + x; if (rx >= W) break;
              const v = m[y * gw + x], q = ry * W + rx;
              if (v > g[q]) g[q] = v;
            }
          }
        }
      }

      if (!grids.size) {
        setStatus('No objects detected. · Không nhận diện được vật thể.', 'var(--warning)');
        runBtn.disabled = false; return;
      }

      const segGrids = [...grids.entries()].map(([label, grid]) => ({ label, grid }));
      buildLabelMap(segGrids, depOut, wantPlanes, W, H);
      drawPreview();
      $('controls')?.classList.remove('hidden');
      $('legend')?.classList.remove('hidden');
      $('s3wrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
        $('samwrap')?.classList.remove('hidden');
      const secs = ((performance.now() - t0) / 1000).toFixed(1);
      setStatus(`Done in ${secs}s. · Xong sau ${secs}s.`, 'var(--success)');
    } catch (err: any) {
      console.error(err);
      // Show the real cause — a generic line hides everything and makes the
      // failure unreportable.
      const detail = String(err?.message ?? err).slice(0, 160);
      setStatus(
        `Failed: ${detail} — try again; if it repeats, reload the page. · Lỗi: ${detail} — thử lại; nếu lặp lại, tải lại trang.`,
        'var(--danger)'
      );
    } finally {
      runBtn.disabled = false;
    }
  });

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- helpers
  function canvasOfImage(img: HTMLImageElement) {
    const c = document.createElement('canvas');
    c.width = img.naturalWidth; c.height = img.naturalHeight;
    c.getContext('2d')!.drawImage(img, 0, 0);
    return c;
  }

  // Resize a single-channel RawImage to the work grid; returns Uint8 length W*H.
  function channelToGrid(raw: any, W: number, H: number, smooth: boolean): Uint8Array {
    const nat = document.createElement('canvas');
    nat.width = raw.width; nat.height = raw.height;
    const nctx = nat.getContext('2d')!;
    const id = nctx.createImageData(raw.width, raw.height);
    const ch = raw.channels ?? 1;
    for (let i = 0; i < raw.width * raw.height; i++) {
      const v = raw.data[i * ch];
      id.data[i * 4] = v; id.data[i * 4 + 1] = v; id.data[i * 4 + 2] = v; id.data[i * 4 + 3] = 255;
    }
    nctx.putImageData(id, 0, 0);
    const g = document.createElement('canvas');
    g.width = W; g.height = H;
    const gctx = g.getContext('2d')!;
    gctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = smooth;
    gctx.drawImage(nat, 0, 0, W, H);
    const out = new Uint8Array(W * H);
    const d = gctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data;
    for (let i = 0; i < W * H; i++) out[i] = d[i * 4];
    return out;
  }

  function boxBlur(a: Float32Array, W: number, H: number, r: number) {
    const tmp = new Float32Array(a.length);
    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
      let s = 0, n = 0;
      for (let k = -r; k <= r; k++) { const xx = x + k; if (xx >= 0 && xx < W) { s += a[y * W + xx]; n++; } }
      tmp[y * W + x] = s / n;
    }
    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {
      let s = 0, n = 0;
      for (let k = -r; k <= r; k++) { const yy = y + k; if (yy >= 0 && yy < H) { s += tmp[yy * W + x]; n++; } }
      a[y * W + x] = s / n;
    }
  }

  function hsv(h: number, s: number, v: number): [number, number, number] {
    const c = v * s, x = c * (1 - Math.abs(((h / 60) % 2) - 1)), m = v - c;
    let r = 0, g = 0, b = 0;
    if (h < 60) [r, g, b] = [c, x, 0]; else if (h < 120) [r, g, b] = [x, c, 0];
    else if (h < 180) [r, g, b] = [0, c, x]; else if (h < 240) [r, g, b] = [0, x, c];
    else if (h < 300) [r, g, b] = [x, 0, c]; else [r, g, b] = [c, 0, x];
    return [Math.round((r + m) * 255), Math.round((g + m) * 255), Math.round((b + m) * 255)];
  }

  // Grab the source image as an RGB byte array at an arbitrary resolution.
  function srcRGB(W: number, H: number): Uint8Array {
    const c = document.createElement('canvas');
    c.width = W; c.height = H;
    const ctx = c.getContext('2d')!;
    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true;
    ctx.drawImage(sourceImage!, 0, 0, W, H);
    const d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data;
    const out = new Uint8Array(W * H * 3);
    for (let i = 0, j = 0; i < W * H; i++, j += 3) { out[j] = d[i * 4]; out[j + 1] = d[i * 4 + 1]; out[j + 2] = d[i * 4 + 2]; }
    return out;
  }

  /**
   * Bilateral majority vote: replace each label with the dominant label among
   * neighbours that are similar in BOTH the render's colour and its depth.
   * A colour edge OR a depth edge counts as a boundary, so this snaps wavy
   * semantic boundaries onto the real geometry — and, crucially, still finds
   * the ceiling/wall or floor/wall corner even when the two surfaces are the
   * same beige colour, because the depth jumps there.
   */
  function bilateralRefine(labels: Int32Array, src: Uint8Array, depth: Float32Array | null, W: number, H: number, iters: number, R: number, Sc: number, Sd: number) {
    const N = W * H;
    let cur = labels;
    let maxL = 0; for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) if (cur[i] > maxL) maxL = cur[i];
    const votes = new Float32Array(maxL + 2);
    const touched = new Int32Array((2 * R + 1) * (2 * R + 1));
    for (let it = 0; it < iters; it++) {
      const next = new Int32Array(N);
      for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
        const p = y * W + x, pj = p * 3;
        const pr = src[pj], pg = src[pj + 1], pb = src[pj + 2], pd = depth ? depth[p] : 0;
        let nt = 0, best = cur[p], bestv = -1;
        for (let dy = -R; dy <= R; dy++) {
          const yy = y + dy; if (yy < 0 || yy >= H) continue;
          for (let dx = -R; dx <= R; dx++) {
            const xx = x + dx; if (xx < 0 || xx >= W) continue;
            const q = yy * W + xx, l = cur[q]; if (l < 0) continue;
            const qj = q * 3, dr = pr - src[qj], dg = pg - src[qj + 1], db = pb - src[qj + 2];
            let w = 1 / (1 + (dr * dr + dg * dg + db * db) / Sc);
            if (depth) { const dd = pd - depth[q]; w *= 1 / (1 + (dd * dd) / Sd); }
            if (votes[l] === 0) touched[nt++] = l;
            votes[l] += w;
          }
        }
        for (let k = 0; k < nt; k++) { const l = touched[k]; if (votes[l] > bestv) { bestv = votes[l]; best = l; } votes[l] = 0; }
        next[p] = best;
      }
      cur = next;
    }
    return cur;
  }

  // N well-separated colours (golden-angle hue) for giving every region a
  // unique colour — so selecting by colour in Photoshop never picks up two
  // different surfaces (the ceiling and the floor were both red before this).
  function buildPalette(n: number): [number, number, number][] {
    const p: [number, number, number][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) p.push(hsv((i * 137.508) % 360, 0.86 - (i % 3) * 0.12, 0.99 - (i % 2) * 0.16));
    return p;
  }

  // -------------------------------------- the core: build the label map
  function buildLabelMap(
    segGrids: Array<{ label: string; grid: Uint8Array }>,
    depOut: any,
    wantPlanes: boolean,
    W: number,
    H: number
  ) {
    const origW = sourceImage!.naturalWidth, origH = sourceImage!.naturalHeight;
    const N = W * H;
    const srcW = srcRGB(W, H);

    // 1. argmax class per pixel (full coverage, no holes)
    let classIdx = new Int32Array(N).fill(-1);
    const bestVal = new Uint8Array(N);
    const classNames: string[] = [];
    for (const seg of segGrids) {
      const k = classNames.length;
      classNames.push(seg.label);
      const m = seg.grid; // already merged at work resolution
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) if (m[i] > bestVal[i]) { bestVal[i] = m[i]; classIdx[i] = k; }
    }

    // depth grid first — it also guides the boundary refinement
    let depthGrid: Float32Array | null = null;
    if (depOut) {
      const raw = depOut.depth ?? depOut.predicted_depth ?? depOut;
      depthGrid = Float32Array.from(channelToGrid(raw, W, H, true));
      boxBlur(depthGrid, W, H, 3);
    }

    // 1b. snap the coarse class boundaries onto the render's real edges —
    // colour edges AND depth edges, so same-coloured ceiling/wall corners hold
    classIdx = bilateralRefine(classIdx, srcW, depthGrid, W, H, 3, 3, 1400, 18) as typeof classIdx;

    // 1c. furniture standing flush against a wall (her lower cabinet under the
    // artwork) often gets classed as "wall". It sits NEARER the camera than
    // the wall plane behind it, so carve out wall pixels that are markedly
    // nearer than the robust wall depth of their column.
    const raisedK = classNames.length;
    classNames.push('object at wall');
    if (depthGrid) {
      const colMed = new Float32Array(W).fill(NaN);
      const tmpD: number[] = [];
      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
        tmpD.length = 0;
        for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {
          const p = y * W + x;
          const nm = classNames[classIdx[p]];
          if (nm && WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm))) tmpD.push(depthGrid[p]);
        }
        if (tmpD.length >= H * 0.08) { tmpD.sort((a, b) => a - b); colMed[x] = tmpD[tmpD.length >> 1]; }
      }
      // spread of residuals → robust threshold
      const res: number[] = [];
      for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
        const nm = classNames[classIdx[p]];
        if (!nm || !WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm))) continue;
        const m = colMed[p % W]; if (Number.isNaN(m)) continue;
        res.push(Math.abs(depthGrid[p] - m));
      }
      res.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const mad = res.length ? res[res.length >> 1] : 3;
      const Tp = Math.max(mad * 4, 10); // depth units are 0..255 inverse depth
      for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
        const nm = classNames[classIdx[p]];
        if (!nm || !WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm))) continue;
        const m = colMed[p % W]; if (Number.isNaN(m)) continue;
        if (depthGrid[p] - m > Tp) classIdx[p] = raisedK; // nearer = brighter
      }
    }

    // 2. wall-plane split — WALLS ONLY, decided PER COLUMN, not per pixel.
    // Wall corners in an interior are near-vertical lines, so classifying
    // whole columns is far more robust than thresholding noisy per-pixel
    // gradients (which left all three walls one colour on a real render),
    // and it produces perfectly straight vertical plane boundaries.
    const bucket = new Uint8Array(N);
    if (wantPlanes && depthGrid) {
      const gx = new Float32Array(N);
      for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
        const i = y * W + x;
        gx[i] = depthGrid[y * W + Math.min(x + 2, W - 1)] - depthGrid[y * W + Math.max(x - 2, 0)];
      }

      // robust per-column wall slope: median of gx over the wall pixels there
      const colSlope = new Float32Array(W).fill(NaN);
      const tmp: number[] = [];
      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
        tmp.length = 0;
        for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {
          const p = y * W + x;
          const nm = classNames[classIdx[p]];
          if (nm && WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm))) tmp.push(gx[p]);
        }
        if (tmp.length >= H * 0.05) {
          tmp.sort((a, b) => a - b);
          colSlope[x] = tmp[tmp.length >> 1];
        }
      }
      // fill gaps (columns with no wall) from the nearest valid neighbour
      let last = NaN;
      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { if (Number.isNaN(colSlope[x])) colSlope[x] = last; else last = colSlope[x]; }
      last = NaN;
      for (let x = W - 1; x >= 0; x--) { if (Number.isNaN(colSlope[x])) colSlope[x] = last; else last = colSlope[x]; }

      // smooth the 1D signal
      const sm = new Float32Array(W);
      const SR = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * 0.01));
      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
        let s = 0, n = 0;
        for (let k = -SR; k <= SR; k++) { const xx = x + k; if (xx >= 0 && xx < W && !Number.isNaN(colSlope[xx])) { s += colSlope[xx]; n++; } }
        sm[x] = n ? s / n : 0;
      }

      // threshold from robust spread (median absolute deviation)
      const absDev = [...sm].map(Math.abs).sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const mad = absDev[absDev.length >> 1] || 0.1;
      const T = Math.max(mad * 1.2, 0.15);

      // classify columns, then clean up: median filter + minimum run length,
      // so the wall splits into a few solid vertical bands, not flicker
      const colClass = new Uint8Array(W);
      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) colClass[x] = sm[x] < -T ? 0 : sm[x] > T ? 2 : 1;
      const MIN_RUN = Math.max(4, Math.round(W * 0.06));
      let runStart = 0;
      for (let x = 1; x <= W; x++) {
        if (x === W || colClass[x] !== colClass[runStart]) {
          if (x - runStart < MIN_RUN) {
            const fill = runStart > 0 ? colClass[runStart - 1] : (x < W ? colClass[x] : colClass[runStart]);
            for (let k = runStart; k < x; k++) colClass[k] = fill;
          }
          runStart = x;
        }
      }

      for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
        const nm = classNames[classIdx[p]];
        if (nm && WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm))) bucket[p] = colClass[p % W];
      }
    }

    // 3. connected components over (classIdx, bucket)
    const comp = new Int32Array(N).fill(-1);
    const compClass: number[] = [];
    const compBucket: number[] = [];
    const compSize: number[] = [];
    const stack = new Int32Array(N);
    let nComp = 0;
    for (let s = 0; s < N; s++) {
      if (comp[s] !== -1 || classIdx[s] < 0) continue;
      const ck = classIdx[s], bk = bucket[s], id = nComp++;
      compClass.push(ck); compBucket.push(bk); let size = 0, sp = 0;
      stack[sp++] = s; comp[s] = id;
      while (sp > 0) {
        const p = stack[--sp]; size++;
        const x = p % W, y = (p / W) | 0;
        if (x > 0) { const q = p - 1; if (comp[q] === -1 && classIdx[q] === ck && bucket[q] === bk) { comp[q] = id; stack[sp++] = q; } }
        if (x < W - 1) { const q = p + 1; if (comp[q] === -1 && classIdx[q] === ck && bucket[q] === bk) { comp[q] = id; stack[sp++] = q; } }
        if (y > 0) { const q = p - W; if (comp[q] === -1 && classIdx[q] === ck && bucket[q] === bk) { comp[q] = id; stack[sp++] = q; } }
        if (y < H - 1) { const q = p + W; if (comp[q] === -1 && classIdx[q] === ck && bucket[q] === bk) { comp[q] = id; stack[sp++] = q; } }
      }
      compSize.push(size);
    }

    // 4. merge speckle into the neighbour with the longest shared border.
    // Two thresholds: architectural fragments fold aggressively (0.4% of the
    // frame), but small OBJECTS survive down to 0.02% — folding a bottle or a
    // spotlight into the wall behind it is how small decor used to vanish.
    const minArch = Math.max(48, Math.round(N * 0.004));
    const minObj = Math.max(16, Math.round(N * 0.0002));
    const isArchName = (nm?: string) => !!nm && (WALL_LIKE.has(first(nm)) || FLOOR_CEIL.has(first(nm)));
    const remap = new Int32Array(nComp);
    for (let i = 0; i < nComp; i++) remap[i] = i;
    const find = (a: number) => { while (remap[a] !== a) a = remap[a] = remap[remap[a]]; return a; };
    const edges = new Map<number, Map<number, number>>();
    const addEdge = (a: number, b: number) => { if (a === b) return; if (!edges.has(a)) edges.set(a, new Map()); const m = edges.get(a)!; m.set(b, (m.get(b) ?? 0) + 1); };
    for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
      const a = comp[p]; if (a < 0) continue;
      const x = p % W, y = (p / W) | 0;
      if (x < W - 1) { const b = comp[p + 1]; if (b >= 0 && b !== a) { addEdge(a, b); addEdge(b, a); } }
      if (y < H - 1) { const b = comp[p + W]; if (b >= 0 && b !== a) { addEdge(a, b); addEdge(b, a); } }
    }
    const order = [...Array(nComp).keys()].sort((a, b) => compSize[a] - compSize[b]);
    for (const cId of order) {
      const lim = isArchName(classNames[compClass[cId]]) ? minArch : minObj;
      if (compSize[find(cId)] >= lim) continue;
      const nbrs = edges.get(cId); if (!nbrs || !nbrs.size) continue;
      let best = -1, bestLen = -1;
      for (const [nb, len] of nbrs) { const r = find(nb); if (r === find(cId)) continue; if (len > bestLen) { bestLen = len; best = r; } }
      if (best >= 0) { const rc = find(cId); compSize[best] += compSize[rc]; remap[rc] = best; }
    }

    // 4b. compact regions to a dense root index
    const rootIndex = new Map<number, number>();
    const rootClass: number[] = [];
    const rootBucket: number[] = [];
    const rootSize: number[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < nComp; i++) {
      if (find(i) !== i) continue;
      rootIndex.set(i, rootIndex.size);
      rootClass.push(compClass[i]); rootBucket.push(compBucket[i]); rootSize.push(compSize[i]);
    }
    const nReg = rootIndex.size;
    const regionOf = new Int32Array(N);
    for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) { const a = comp[p]; regionOf[p] = a >= 0 ? rootIndex.get(find(a))! : -1; }

    // 4c. architecture meets along straight lines, but the segmenter returns
    // wavy blobs — the ceiling–wall and floor–wall borders come out rippled.
    // Measure the border per column, fit a piecewise-straight polyline through
    // it, and re-partition the two classes across the fitted line. Only pixels
    // of those two classes are ever reassigned, so furniture and fixtures that
    // occlude the border are left untouched.
    {
      const regCat = new Int8Array(nReg); // 0 other · 1 ceiling · 2 wall · 3 floor
      for (let r = 0; r < nReg; r++) {
        const nm = first(classNames[rootClass[r]] ?? '');
        if (WALL_LIKE.has(nm)) regCat[r] = 2;
        else if (GROUP[nm] === 'ceiling') regCat[r] = 1;
        else if (GROUP[nm] === 'floor') regCat[r] = 3;
      }
      straightenArchBoundary(regionOf, W, H, regCat, 1, 2, 'top');    // ceiling over wall
      straightenArchBoundary(regionOf, W, H, regCat, 2, 3, 'bottom'); // wall over floor
    }

    // 5. colour like a material pass, with the FIXED schema palette: the same
    // group is the same colour on every run, on every image — left wall teal,
    // ceiling dark red, lighting fixtures pure white. Tiny non-architectural
    // fragments (<0.1% of frame) collapse into the generic decor colour
    // instead of pretending to be a confident detection.
    const tinyDecor = Math.round(N * 0.001);
    const keyOfRegion = (r: number): string => {
      const nm = first(classNames[rootClass[r]] ?? 'unknown');
      if (WALL_LIKE.has(nm)) return `wall|${rootBucket[r]}`;
      const g = GROUP[nm];
      if (g && !['floor', 'ceiling', 'rug', 'door', 'window', 'arch'].includes(g) && rootSize[r] < tinyDecor)
        return 'decor';
      return g ?? `x:${nm}`;
    };
    // stable fallback for unmapped classes: hue from the class name hash
    const fallbackColor = (key: string): [number, number, number] => {
      let h = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < key.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + key.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
      return hsv(h % 360, 0.7, 0.85);
    };
    const regColor: [number, number, number][] = new Array(nReg);
    for (let r = 0; r < nReg; r++) {
      const k = keyOfRegion(r);
      regColor[r] = GROUP_COLOR[k] ?? fallbackColor(k);
    }

    // 6. upscale the region map to full resolution (nearest), then snap the
    //    boundaries to the full-res render edges so lines come out crisp.
    let fullReg = new Int32Array(origW * origH);
    for (let Y = 0; Y < origH; Y++) {
      const wy = Math.min(H - 1, (Y * H / origH) | 0);
      for (let X = 0; X < origW; X++) {
        const wx = Math.min(W - 1, (X * W / origW) | 0);
        fullReg[Y * origW + X] = regionOf[wy * W + wx];
      }
    }
    const srcF = srcRGB(origW, origH);
    fullReg = boundaryRefineRegions(fullReg, srcF, origW, origH, 3, 3, 1200) as typeof fullReg;
    // majority filter: shaves the staircase jaggies left after refinement so
    // long boundaries read as clean lines
    fullReg = modeFilter(fullReg, origW, origH, 2) as typeof fullReg;

    // 7. paint the final solid label map
    labelCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    labelCanvas.width = origW; labelCanvas.height = origH;
    const lctx = labelCanvas.getContext('2d')!;
    const out = lctx.createImageData(origW, origH);
    for (let p = 0; p < origW * origH; p++) {
      const r = fullReg[p];
      const c = r >= 0 ? regColor[r] : [18, 18, 18];
      out.data[p * 4] = c[0]; out.data[p * 4 + 1] = c[1]; out.data[p * 4 + 2] = c[2]; out.data[p * 4 + 3] = 255;
    }
    lctx.putImageData(out, 0, 0);

    // 8. legend, one entry per colour key
    const perKey = new Map<string, { color: [number, number, number]; regions: number; area: number }>();
    for (let r = 0; r < nReg; r++) {
      const key = keyOfRegion(r);
      const e = perKey.get(key) ?? { color: regColor[r], regions: 0, area: 0 };
      e.regions++; e.area += rootSize[r];
      if (!perKey.has(key)) perKey.set(key, e);
    }
    renderLegend(perKey);
  }

  /** 3x3 majority vote on region ids, boundary pixels only — cheap edge polish. */
  function modeFilter(reg: Int32Array, W: number, H: number, iters: number) {
    let cur = reg;
    const ids = new Int32Array(9), cnt = new Int32Array(9);
    for (let it = 0; it < iters; it++) {
      const next = Int32Array.from(cur);
      for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1; x < W - 1; x++) {
        const p = y * W + x, r = cur[p];
        if (cur[p - 1] === r && cur[p + 1] === r && cur[p - W] === r && cur[p + W] === r) continue;
        let n = 0;
        for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {
          const v = cur[(y + dy) * W + (x + dx)];
          let k = 0; for (; k < n; k++) if (ids[k] === v) { cnt[k]++; break; }
          if (k === n) { ids[n] = v; cnt[n] = 1; n++; }
        }
        let best = r, bv = 0;
        for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) if (cnt[k] > bv) { bv = cnt[k]; best = ids[k]; }
        next[p] = best;
      }
      cur = next;
    }
    return cur;
  }

  /** Fit a piecewise-straight polyline through noisy samples: recursive
   *  least-squares split-and-merge. A segment splits only where the SMOOTHED
   *  residual is systematic — a real corner — never on pointwise noise, and
   *  interior knots sit at the intersection of the two neighbouring lines,
   *  which is what a wall corner actually is. */
  function fitPolyline(px: number[], py: number[], tol: number, minSeg: number) {
    const lsq = (a: number, b: number) => {
      let sx = 0, sy = 0, sxx = 0, sxy = 0, n = 0;
      for (let i = a; i <= b; i++) { sx += px[i]; sy += py[i]; sxx += px[i] * px[i]; sxy += px[i] * py[i]; n++; }
      const den = n * sxx - sx * sx;
      const m = den ? (n * sxy - sx * sy) / den : 0;
      return { m, c: (sy - m * sx) / n };
    };
    // prefix sums make the SSE of any straight-line fit O(1), so the best
    // split point of a segment is an O(n) scan
    const n0 = px.length;
    const Px = new Float64Array(n0 + 1), Py = new Float64Array(n0 + 1), Pxx = new Float64Array(n0 + 1),
          Pxy = new Float64Array(n0 + 1), Pyy = new Float64Array(n0 + 1);
    for (let i = 0; i < n0; i++) {
      Px[i + 1] = Px[i] + px[i]; Py[i + 1] = Py[i] + py[i];
      Pxx[i + 1] = Pxx[i] + px[i] * px[i]; Pxy[i + 1] = Pxy[i] + px[i] * py[i]; Pyy[i + 1] = Pyy[i] + py[i] * py[i];
    }
    const sse = (a: number, b: number) => {
      const n = b - a + 1;
      const sx = Px[b + 1] - Px[a], sy = Py[b + 1] - Py[a], sxx = Pxx[b + 1] - Pxx[a],
            sxy = Pxy[b + 1] - Pxy[a], syy = Pyy[b + 1] - Pyy[a];
      const den = n * sxx - sx * sx;
      const m = den ? (n * sxy - sx * sy) / den : 0;
      const c = (sy - m * sx) / n;
      return Math.max(0, syy + m * m * sxx + n * c * c - 2 * m * sxy - 2 * c * sy + 2 * m * c * sx);
    };
    const segs: Array<{ a: number; b: number; m: number; c: number }> = [];
    const stack: Array<[number, number]> = [[0, n0 - 1]];
    while (stack.length && segs.length + stack.length < 9) {
      const [a, b] = stack.pop()!;
      const whole = sse(a, b);
      let split = -1;
      if (b - a + 1 >= minSeg * 2) {
        let best = Infinity;
        for (let i = a + minSeg; i <= b - minSeg; i++) {
          const s = sse(a, i) + sse(i, b);
          if (s < best) { best = s; split = i; }
        }
        // a real corner slashes the error; ripples and noise do not
        if (!(best < whole * 0.5 && whole - best > tol * tol * (b - a + 1) * 0.05)) split = -1;
      }
      if (split > 0) stack.push([a, split], [split, b]);
      else segs.push({ a, b, ...lsq(a, b) });
    }
    while (stack.length) { const [a, b] = stack.pop()!; segs.push({ a, b, ...lsq(a, b) }); }
    segs.sort((s, t) => s.a - t.a);
    const kx: number[] = [px[segs[0].a]];
    const ky: number[] = [segs[0].m * kx[0] + segs[0].c];
    for (let s = 1; s < segs.length; s++) {
      const L = segs[s - 1], R = segs[s];
      const bx = px[R.a];
      let ix = (R.c - L.c) / (L.m - R.m);
      // near-parallel or far-away intersection → just butt-join at the split
      if (!Number.isFinite(ix) || Math.abs(ix - bx) > (px[L.b] - px[L.a] + px[R.b] - px[R.a]) / 4) {
        kx.push(bx); ky.push((L.m * bx + L.c + R.m * bx + R.c) / 2);
      } else { kx.push(ix); ky.push(L.m * ix + L.c); }
    }
    const last = segs[segs.length - 1];
    kx.push(px[last.b]); ky.push(last.m * px[last.b] + last.c);
    return { kx, ky };
  }

  /** Straighten the border between two architectural categories (catAbove at
   *  smaller y). `anchor` names the frame edge the reference class hangs from:
   *  the ceiling is measured walking down from the top, the floor walking up
   *  from the bottom. Columns where an object hides the border are bridged by
   *  the fitted polyline; only pixels of the two categories are reassigned. */
  function straightenArchBoundary(
    reg: Int32Array, W: number, H: number, regCat: Int8Array,
    catAbove: number, catBelow: number, anchor: 'top' | 'bottom'
  ) {
    const cat = (p: number) => { const r = reg[p]; return r >= 0 ? regCat[r] : 0; };
    const GAP = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * 0.03)); // thin trim between the two is fine
    const yBnd = new Float32Array(W).fill(NaN);
    const aboveReg = new Int32Array(W).fill(-1);
    const belowReg = new Int32Array(W).fill(-1);
    const dir = anchor === 'top' ? 1 : -1;
    const anchoredCat = anchor === 'top' ? catAbove : catBelow;
    const partnerCat = anchor === 'top' ? catBelow : catAbove;

    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
      // the anchored class must start at its frame edge (small slack for crops)
      let y = anchor === 'top' ? 0 : H - 1, slack = GAP;
      while (slack-- > 0 && y >= 0 && y < H && cat(y * W + x) !== anchoredCat) y += dir;
      if (y < 0 || y >= H || cat(y * W + x) !== anchoredCat) continue;
      while (y + dir >= 0 && y + dir < H && cat((y + dir) * W + x) === anchoredCat) y += dir;
      const yEnd = y;
      let yPartner = -1;
      for (let k = 1; k <= GAP; k++) {
        const yy = yEnd + dir * k; if (yy < 0 || yy >= H) break;
        const c = cat(yy * W + x);
        if (c === partnerCat) { yPartner = yy; break; }
        if (c === anchoredCat) break;
      }
      if (yPartner < 0) continue; // border occluded here — the polyline bridges it
      yBnd[x] = (yEnd + yPartner) / 2;
      if (anchor === 'top') { aboveReg[x] = reg[yEnd * W + x]; belowReg[x] = reg[yPartner * W + x]; }
      else { belowReg[x] = reg[yEnd * W + x]; aboveReg[x] = reg[yPartner * W + x]; }
    }

    // median-smooth the measured border: single-column spikes are seg noise
    const yMed = new Float32Array(W).fill(NaN);
    const win: number[] = [];
    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
      if (Number.isNaN(yBnd[x])) continue;
      win.length = 0;
      for (let k = -3; k <= 3; k++) { const xx = x + k; if (xx >= 0 && xx < W && !Number.isNaN(yBnd[xx])) win.push(yBnd[xx]); }
      win.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      yMed[x] = win[win.length >> 1];
    }

    const valid: number[] = [];
    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) if (!Number.isNaN(yMed[x])) valid.push(x);
    if (valid.length < 2) return;

    // spans of measurable border; a very wide occluder splits the border in two
    const maxGap = Math.round(W * 0.25), minSpan = Math.round(W * 0.1);
    const spans: Array<[number, number]> = [];
    let s0 = 0;
    for (let i = 1; i <= valid.length; i++) {
      if (i === valid.length || valid[i] - valid[i - 1] > maxGap) {
        if (valid[i - 1] - valid[s0] >= minSpan) spans.push([s0, i - 1]);
        s0 = i;
      }
    }

    const eps = Math.max(2, H * 0.012);
    for (const [i0, i1] of spans) {
      const px: number[] = [], py: number[] = [];
      for (let i = i0; i <= i1; i++) { px.push(valid[i]); py.push(yMed[valid[i]]); }
      const { kx, ky } = fitPolyline(px, py, eps, Math.max(6, Math.round(W * 0.05)));
      const x0 = px[0], x1 = px[px.length - 1];
      const f = new Float32Array(x1 - x0 + 1);
      let seg = 0;
      for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) {
        while (seg < kx.length - 2 && x > kx[seg + 1]) seg++;
        const xa = kx[seg], ya = ky[seg], xb = kx[seg + 1], yb = ky[seg + 1];
        f[x - x0] = xb === xa ? ya : ya + (yb - ya) * (x - xa) / (xb - xa);
      }
      let maxDev = 0;
      for (let i = i0; i <= i1; i++) maxDev = Math.max(maxDev, Math.abs(yMed[valid[i]] - f[valid[i] - x0]));
      if (maxDev > H * 0.12) continue; // genuinely irregular — do not force it

      // re-partition inside a band around the fitted line
      const Wr = Math.min(H * 0.15, maxDev + GAP + 2);
      for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) {
        const fb = f[x - x0];
        const yLo = Math.max(0, Math.floor(fb - Wr)), yHi = Math.min(H - 1, Math.ceil(fb + Wr));
        // targets: the nearest pixel of each class just off the line in THIS
        // column keeps wall-plane buckets intact; fall back to the measured one
        let ar = aboveReg[x], br = belowReg[x];
        for (let y = Math.min(yHi, Math.floor(fb)); y >= yLo; y--) { const p = y * W + x; if (cat(p) === catAbove) { ar = reg[p]; break; } }
        for (let y = Math.max(yLo, Math.ceil(fb)); y <= yHi; y++) { const p = y * W + x; if (cat(p) === catBelow) { br = reg[p]; break; } }
        for (let y = yLo; y <= yHi; y++) {
          const p = y * W + x, c = cat(p);
          if (y < fb) { if (c === catBelow && ar >= 0) reg[p] = ar; }
          else if (c === catAbove && br >= 0) reg[p] = br;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /** Same bilateral idea, at full resolution, on region ids, boundary pixels only. */
  function boundaryRefineRegions(reg: Int32Array, src: Uint8Array, W: number, H: number, iters: number, R: number, S: number) {
    const N = W * H;
    let maxR = 0; for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) if (reg[i] > maxR) maxR = reg[i];
    const votes = new Float32Array(maxR + 2);
    const touched = new Int32Array((2 * R + 1) * (2 * R + 1));
    let cur = reg;
    for (let it = 0; it < iters; it++) {
      const isB = new Uint8Array(N);
      for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
        const x = p % W, y = (p / W) | 0, r = cur[p];
        if ((x > 0 && cur[p - 1] !== r) || (x < W - 1 && cur[p + 1] !== r) || (y > 0 && cur[p - W] !== r) || (y < H - 1 && cur[p + W] !== r)) isB[p] = 1;
      }
      const next = Int32Array.from(cur);
      for (let p = 0; p < N; p++) {
        if (!isB[p]) continue;
        const x = p % W, y = (p / W) | 0, pj = p * 3;
        const pr = src[pj], pg = src[pj + 1], pb = src[pj + 2];
        let nt = 0, best = cur[p], bestv = -1;
        for (let dy = -R; dy <= R; dy++) {
          const yy = y + dy; if (yy < 0 || yy >= H) continue;
          for (let dx = -R; dx <= R; dx++) {
            const xx = x + dx; if (xx < 0 || xx >= W) continue;
            const q = yy * W + xx, r = cur[q]; if (r < 0) continue;
            const qj = q * 3, dr = pr - src[qj], dg = pg - src[qj + 1], db = pb - src[qj + 2];
            const w = 1 / (1 + (dr * dr + dg * dg + db * db) / S);
            if (votes[r] === 0) touched[nt++] = r;
            votes[r] += w;
          }
        }
        for (let k = 0; k < nt; k++) { const r = touched[k]; if (votes[r] > bestv) { bestv = votes[r]; best = r; } votes[r] = 0; }
        next[p] = best;
      }
      cur = next;
    }
    return cur;
  }

  const KEY_LABELS: Record<string, [string, string]> = {
    'wall|0': ['wall — left', 'tường trái'],
    'wall|1': ['wall — centre', 'tường giữa'],
    'wall|2': ['wall — right', 'tường phải'],
    ceiling: ['ceiling', 'trần'],
    floor: ['floor', 'sàn'],
    rug: ['rug / carpet', 'thảm'],
    soft: ['soft furniture', 'sofa & ghế đệm'],
    tables: ['tables', 'bàn'],
    hard: ['cabinets & consoles', 'tủ & kệ'],
    decor: ['artwork & decor', 'tranh & đồ trang trí'],
    lighting: ['lighting fixtures', 'thiết bị đèn'],
    plant: ['plants', 'cây xanh'],
    door: ['door', 'cửa'],
    window: ['window', 'cửa sổ'],
    arch: ['stairs / columns', 'cầu thang / cột'],
  };

  function renderLegend(perKey: Map<string, { color: number[]; regions: number; area: number }>) {
    const box = $('legendItems'); if (!box) return;
    box.innerHTML = '';
    const items = [...perKey.entries()].sort((a, b) => b[1].area - a[1].area);
    for (const [key, info] of items) {
      const special = KEY_LABELS[key];
      const name = special ? special[0] : key.replace(/^x:/, '');
      const vi = special ? special[1] : VI[key.replace(/^x:/, '')];
      const chip = document.createElement('span');
      chip.className = 'chip';
      chip.innerHTML =
        `<span style="display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;background:rgb(${info.color[0]},${info.color[1]},${info.color[2]})"></span>` +
        `${name}${info.regions > 1 ? ` <span style="opacity:.7">×${info.regions}</span>` : ''}` +
        `${vi ? ` · <span style="color:var(--vi-text)">${vi}</span>` : ''}`;
      box.appendChild(chip);
    }
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------- download
  function download(type: 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg') {
    if (!labelCanvas) return;
    const ext = type === 'image/png' ? 'png' : 'jpg';
    labelCanvas.toBlob((blob) => {
      if (!blob) return;
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      a.download = `labels.${ext}`;
      a.click();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href);
    }, type, type === 'image/jpeg' ? 0.95 : undefined);
  }
  $('dlPng')?.addEventListener('click', () => download('image/png'));
  $('dlJpg')?.addEventListener('click', () => download('image/jpeg'));
</script>
